        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: AI safety event taxonomy — UI dashboard and CLI command",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nThere is no UI or CLI surface for observing AI safety events. Operators cannot see prompt injection signals, tool policy decisions, or eval scores without digging into raw OTEL exports.\n\n## Evidence\n- `openclaw safety events` CLI command added (run `openclaw safety events --help` to see options: `--type`, `--session`, `--since`, `--limit`, `--severity`, `--json`)\n- `ui/src/pages/safety/` — new Lit-based safety page at `/safety` with KPI strip and event table\n- `/safety` route added to sidebar nav\n- `src/infra/safety-event-store.ts` — in-memory ring buffer (10k cap) with cursor-paginated query API\n- `src/gateway/server-methods/safety.ts` — `safety.events.list` and `safety.events.summary` RPC handlers\n- MVP uses in-memory store; SQLite persistence flagged as next step in PR description\n- Depends on: #107176, #107184\n\n## Evidence — Clawsweeper re-review fixes (2026-07-14)\n\n**Rebase:** rebased onto the updated #107184 (which itself carries the #107176 security fix), picking up the untrusted-path exclusion of AI safety events and the OTEL emitter-provenance attributes. Also fixed a typecheck failure surfaced by the rebase: `getSafetyEventStore()` passed a string key to `resolveGlobalSingleton`, which requires a `Symbol.for(...)` key (matches all other call sites). `pnpm tsgo` is clean on this branch.\n\n**4-PR series design note:** the security boundary is deliberate across the stack — #107176 defines the contracts and excludes AI safety events from the untrusted emit surface (type- and runtime-gated); #107184 wires exporters and preserves emitter provenance; #107187 adds the only plugin-facing emission surface, gated by manifest `safetyEventTypes`; this PR adds the UI/CLI observability surfaces. Untrusted path gated, trusted path only.\n\n**OTEL note:** full end-to-end OTEL integration proof requires a running collector, which is not available in CI; exporter behavior is covered by unit tests in #107184.\n",
